WEBVTT

NOTE English descriptions of the on-screen material. This video contains no speech or music.

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.000
EgoDepth-Bench: metric depth for egocentric manipulation.
Camera-2 RGB and its ground-truth point cloud.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
A head-worn capture rig records six synchronized RGB views.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Five active-infrared stereo modules capture depth.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
A shared hardware trigger synchronizes capture at 30 Hz.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Everyday interaction across 37 physical sites.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
941,233 synchronized timestamps, with six RGB views each:
approximately 5.65 million RGB images.

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Tabletop interaction. Six synchronized RGB views
and the camera-2 ground-truth point cloud.

8
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Handling mahjong tiles. Synchronized views and geometry.

9
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Organizing a sofa. Synchronized views and geometry.

10
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Tabletop object handling. Synchronized views and geometry.

11
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Kitchen worktop. Synchronized views and geometry.

12
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Metric ground-truth Z-depth is aligned
with the camera-2 fisheye RGB image.

13
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Capture five synchronized active-IR stereo pairs.

14
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.000
FoundationStereo reconstructs depth in each module.

15
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Onboard depth from the 336L provides a consistency check.

16
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Project and fuse the five depth maps into camera 2.

17
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.000
The result is metric ground truth
aligned with the fisheye RGB image.

18
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Physical validation uses a certified ball-bar
with known sphere geometry and center spacing.

19
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Fixed-radius sphere fitting estimates the sphere centers.

20
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Median absolute center-spacing error: 1.27 mm
across 1,220 accepted measurements.

21
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Depth is evaluated over the full image,
hand regions and manipulated objects.

22
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.000
24 training, 5 validation and 8 test sites.
There is no site overlap between splits.

23
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
MapAnything adaptation uses six RGB views,
calibrated rays and metric rig poses.

24
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Metric AbsRel: 0.708 public to 0.091 fine-tuned.
Equal-weight mean over eight held-out sites; Z = 0.25–2.0 m.

25
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:40.000
EgoDepth-Bench: Benchmarking Metric Depth
for Egocentric Manipulation.
